  "section_notes": "S1 is strict with 24-hour reporting, 48-hour customer notice, and all-incident scope. S2 sets a 55 °C test and 5% limit, gives customers numeric per-model results but no public publication, and allows corrective action/retesting before regulator may restrict sales. S3 requires new units within 24 months and retrofit within 6 years with an alternative escape. S4 requires built-in suppression within 36 months. S5 mandates recall above 8/100k with prompt notices but lacks a serious-injury clause."
